-- A quick market purchase: goods bought in the market, paid for on the spot, in stock at once.
-- track: joint
--
-- The CREATE TABLE / constraint statements are generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/modules/market-purchases/schema.ts. The sections marked "hand-written" are not managed by
-- Drizzle. Reverse with the file of the same name in drizzle/down.
--
-- Why: a shop that is short of stock buys the goods from the market to finish an order. Stock
-- still never goes below zero (the founder's choice, 2026-11-25); what is added is a fast and
-- correct way to bring the goods in first. It is the mirror of the counter sale (0035). The app
-- makes it in one transaction from what is already there, and nothing here posts anything:
--
--   a purchase order, written as a draft with a market_purchases row beside it, then submitted (PO-);
--   the goods received note for all of it, posted: the goods come into the warehouse at the
--   order's cost (GR-);
--   the supplier's bill for those goods at that cost, with no input tax and nothing withheld,
--   posted (PB-);
--   the payment out of a cash or bank account that settles the bill in full, posted (PV-).
--
-- The seller is a supplier on the list, or someone in the market who is not. For those, each
-- company has one supplier that stands for every such seller, made the first time it is needed
-- by app.market_supplier(): an unregistered individual. The seller's name and phone are typed on
-- the purchase and kept here.
--
-- A seller nobody can name again is given no credit and no tax standing: the market supplier is
-- ordered from, and billed by, only through a quick market purchase, which pays at once; and it
-- is never archived, registered for tax, or given an NTN, STRN or CNIC (input tax is claimed
-- only from a registered supplier, and none is claimed here).
--
-- A quick market purchase is whole when its transaction ends: its submitted order, the posted
-- note that received all of it, the posted bill for exactly those goods at the order's total
-- with no tax on it and nothing withheld, and the posted payment that settles that bill in
-- full; or the transaction is refused. What comes after follows the documents' own rules: goods
-- that go back are a supplier return, and a payment entered by mistake is cancelled and paid
-- again, as for any supplier.
--
-- Database error codes (the buying range, SE200 to SE299):
--   SE267  the market seller is bought from only through a quick market purchase, paid at once
--   SE268  a quick market purchase is written once and whole, and never changed or removed
--   SE269  the market seller is not archived, registered for tax or given a tax identity

